==Enemy==
Project A has the same range as Master A, but his attacks are considerably weaker, albeit with a 20% chance of warping cats back by 500 range.

==Strategy==
As with most Master A. variants, Project A is best dealt with fast units or those that outrange him, and an element of luck is needed due to his Warp. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] can quickly remove him from the battlefield if there is an opening. If you have tanky and heavy-hitting cats or any [[:Category:Cats with Warp Immunity|Cats with Warp Immunity]], bring them, as they can tank his tongue and hit him where it hurts. [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Rover Cat]] is a potent meatshield against him, and any other [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] cat with sufficient health or range will also be of use; [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cat]] is recommended, especially if his [[True Form]] and Immune to Warp [[Talents|Talent]] have been unlocked. [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] may be a good idea as long as Project A doesn't knock it back continuously before Can Can can get to him.

[[Miter Saw Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Miter Saw Cat]] can make short work of this enemy if there isn't any relevant support from non-alien enemies due to his massive DPS against aliens, his resistance against them, and his Immunity to Warp

[[Mekako Saionji (Uber Rare Cat)|Mission Control Mekako]] helps a lot, being tanky and having Massive Damage against Aliens. [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Megaphrodite]] excels against Project A, as she can snipe him from a distance.

Project A's Warp ability may also be exploited. Many rushers, such as [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Sanada Yukimura]] or [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]], have long backswing animations as their only delay between attacks, which is reset by Warp, allowing them to strike again and possibly defeat Project A, provided if he doesn't Warp them again.

